    <!-- Link handling -->
    <string name="vm_link_open_title">Link handling</string>
    <string name="vm_link_open_intro">Tap a drive share link in a browser or another app and the system will ask which app to use — pick \"YunX\" and check \"Always\", then links will open here for parsing.</string>
    <string name="vm_link_open_verified_zero">The \"Verified links\" entry in system settings will always stay at 0: verification requires hosting this app\'s verification file (assetlinks.json) on every drive domain\'s server, and none of those domains belong to this project, so a third-party app cannot do it (enabling automatic verification may even make YunX disappear from the chooser entirely).</string>
    <string name="vm_link_open_manual_associate">The official workaround for third-party apps that cannot verify domains is to associate domains manually: in the system\'s \"Default opening → Open supported links\", check the drive domains for YunX. It works the same as verification (no more chooser), but is recorded under \"Links to open in this app\".</string>
    <string name="vm_link_open_disable_hint">Turning an item off = stop handling that kind of link (the system will hand it back to the browser or the drive\'s official app); changes take effect immediately, no restart needed.</string>
    <string name="vm_link_open_open_settings">Associate domains in system settings</string>
    <string name="vm_link_open_settings_desc">Open \"Default opening → Open supported links\" and check the drive domains you want YunX to handle</string>
